    "breadcrumb": "수리전자물리학 \u003e Tensor analysis \u003e Calculus",
    "content": "1. Scalar gradient $$\r\\nabla\\varphi\r=\\frac{\\partial \\varphi}{\\partial\\vec{u}}\r=\\frac{\\partial \\varphi}{\\partial u_i}\\hat{u}_i\r=\\frac{\\partial \\varphi}{\\partial u_1}\\hat{u}_1+\\frac{\\partial \\varphi}{\\partial u_2}\\hat{u}_+\\frac{\\partial \\varphi}{\\partial u_3}\\hat{u}_3\r$$$$\r[\\nabla\\varphi]_i\r=[\\nabla]_i\\varphi\r=\\frac{\\partial \\varphi}{\\partial u_i}\r$$ 2. Vector Gradient $$\r\\nabla\\vec{f}\r=\\frac{\\partial \\vec{f}}{\\partial\\vec{u}}\r=\\frac{\\partial f_j}{\\partial u_i}\\hat{u}_i\\hat{u}_j\r$$$$\r[\\nabla\\vec{f}]_{ij}\r=[\\nabla]_i\\vec{f}_j\r=\\frac{\\partial f_j}{\\partial u_i}\r$$전개하면, 다음과 같으며, 2차 텐서임을 알 수 있다.\n$$\r\\begin{align}\r\\nabla\\vec{f}\r= \u0026 \\frac{\\partial f_1}{\\partial u_1}\\hat{u}_1\\hat{u}_1 + \\frac{\\partial f_1}{\\partial u_2}\\hat{u}_2\\hat{u}_1 + \\frac{\\partial f_1}{\\partial u_3}\\hat{u}_3\\hat{u}_1 \\\\\r\u0026 \\frac{\\partial f_2}{\\partial u_1}\\hat{u}_1\\hat{u}_2 + \\frac{\\partial f_2}{\\partial u_2}\\hat{u}_2\\hat{u}_2 + \\frac{\\partial f_2}{\\partial u_3}\\hat{u}_3\\hat{u}_2 \\\\\r\u0026 \\frac{\\partial f_3}{\\partial u_1}\\hat{u}_1\\hat{u}_3 + \\frac{\\partial f_3}{\\partial u_2}\\hat{u}_2\\hat{u}_3 + \\frac{\\partial f_3}{\\partial u_3}\\hat{u}_3\\hat{u}_3\r\\end{align}\r$$ 3. Conjugate vector gradient $$\r\\vec{f}\\nabla\r= f_i\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial u_j}\\hat{u}_i\\hat{u}_j\r$$ 4. Vector gradient \u0026 Kronecker delta $$\r\\nabla\\vec{u}\r=\\frac{\\partial \\vec{u}}{\\partial \\vec{u}}\r=\\frac{\\partial u_i}{\\partial u_j}\\hat{u}_i\\hat{u}_j\r=[\\delta_{ij}]\r=\\bar{\\bar{I}}\r$$$$\r[\\nabla\\vec{u}]_{ij}\r=\\partial_i u_j\r=\\bar{\\bar{I}}\r$$ 5. High tensor gradient 2차 텐서에서,\n$$\r\\nabla\\bar{\\bar{A}}\r=\\frac{\\partial \\bar{\\bar{A}}}{\\partial \\vec{u}}\r=\\frac{\\partial A_{jk}}{\\partial u_i}\\hat{u}_i\\hat{u}_j\\hat{u}_k\r$$$$\r[\\nabla\\bar{\\bar{A}}]_{ijk}\r=[\\nabla]_i[\\bar{\\bar{A}}]_{jk}\r=\\frac{\\partial A_{jk}}{\\partial u_i}\r$$4차 텐서에서,\n$$\r\\nabla\\stackrel{4}{A}\r=\\frac{\\partial A_{jklm}}{\\partial u_i}\\hat{u}_i\\hat{u}_j\\hat{u}_k\\hat{u}_l\\hat{u}_m\r$$$$\r[\\nabla\\stackrel{4}{A}]_{ijklm}\r[\\nabla]_i[\\stackrel{4}{A}]_{jklm}\r=\\frac{\\partial A_{jklm}}{\\partial u_i}\\hat{u}_i\\hat{u}_j\\hat{u}_k\\hat{u}_l\\hat{u}_m\r$$",
    "description": "1. Scalar gradient $$\r\\nabla\\varphi\r=\\frac{\\partial \\varphi}{\\partial\\vec{u}}\r=\\frac{\\partial \\varphi}{\\partial u_i}\\hat{u}_i\r=\\frac{\\partial \\varphi}{\\partial u_1}\\hat{u}_1+\\frac{\\partial \\varphi}{\\partial u_2}\\hat{u}_+\\frac{\\partial \\varphi}{\\partial u_3}\\hat{u}_3\r$$$$\r[\\nabla\\varphi]_i\r=[\\nabla]_i\\varphi\r=\\frac{\\partial \\varphi}{\\partial u_i}\r$$ 2. Vector Gradient $$\r\\nabla\\vec{f}\r=\\frac{\\partial \\vec{f}}{\\partial\\vec{u}}\r=\\frac{\\partial f_j}{\\partial u_i}\\hat{u}_i\\hat{u}_j\r$$$$\r[\\nabla\\vec{f}]_{ij}\r=[\\nabla]_i\\vec{f}_j\r=\\frac{\\partial f_j}{\\partial u_i}\r$$전개하면, 다음과 같으며, 2차 텐서임을 알 수 있다.\n$$\r\\begin{align}\r\\nabla\\vec{f}\r= \u0026 \\frac{\\partial f_1}{\\partial u_1}\\hat{u}_1\\hat{u}_1 + \\frac{\\partial f_1}{\\partial u_2}\\hat{u}_2\\hat{u}_1 + \\frac{\\partial f_1}{\\partial u_3}\\hat{u}_3\\hat{u}_1 \\\\\r\u0026 \\frac{\\partial f_2}{\\partial u_1}\\hat{u}_1\\hat{u}_2 + \\frac{\\partial f_2}{\\partial u_2}\\hat{u}_2\\hat{u}_2 + \\frac{\\partial f_2}{\\partial u_3}\\hat{u}_3\\hat{u}_2 \\\\\r\u0026 \\frac{\\partial f_3}{\\partial u_1}\\hat{u}_1\\hat{u}_3 + \\frac{\\partial f_3}{\\partial u_2}\\hat{u}_2\\hat{u}_3 + \\frac{\\partial f_3}{\\partial u_3}\\hat{u}_3\\hat{u}_3\r\\end{align}\r$$ 3. Conjugate vector gradient $$\r\\vec{f}\\nabla\r= f_i\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial u_j}\\hat{u}_i\\hat{u}_j\r$$ 4. Vector gradient \u0026 Kronecker delta $$\r\\nabla\\vec{u}\r=\\frac{\\partial \\vec{u}}{\\partial \\vec{u}}\r=\\frac{\\partial u_i}{\\partial u_j}\\hat{u}_i\\hat{u}_j\r=[\\delta_{ij}]\r=\\bar{\\bar{I}}\r$$$$\r[\\nabla\\vec{u}]_{ij}\r=\\partial_i u_j\r=\\bar{\\bar{I}}\r$$ 5. High tensor gradient 2차 텐서에서,",
